GOAL: Manually deploy Flask app on EC2 using Docker
COMMANDS: see commands/aws.txt + commands/docker.txt

1. SSH into EC2:
   chmod 400 ~/.ssh/devops-key.pem
   ssh -i ~/.ssh/devops-key.pem ubuntu@YOUR_PUBLIC_IP

2. Get your code onto EC2 (choose one):
   Option A - clone from GitHub:
     git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/REPO.git
     cd REPO

   Option B - copy from local machine:
     (run on LOCAL machine, not EC2)
     scp -i ~/.ssh/devops-key.pem -r ~/project/ ubuntu@YOUR_IP:~/

3. Build image on EC2:
   docker build -t flask-api:v1 .

4. Run container:
   docker run -d -p 5000:5000 --restart=always --name flask-api flask-api:v1

5. Verify on EC2:
   docker ps
   curl http://localhost:5000/api/health

6. Verify from YOUR LOCAL machine:
   curl http://YOUR_EC2_IP:5000/api/health
   curl http://YOUR_EC2_IP:5000/api/students

7. If container already exists error:
   docker stop flask-api || true
   docker rm flask-api || true
   (rerun step 4)

8. If app not reachable from internet:
   → Check Security Group in AWS console has port 5000 open
   → Check docker ps shows container is running
   → Check curl localhost:5000 works from inside EC2
